{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yywtbiki42ctlyu2oxiaylo6cwrn4og6wdww4fswnzbynsneswsq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification PASS — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte. No behavioural fixes were needed.**\n\nThe whole C library is one 9-line function (`void sieve(int)`: print, break if `val % 10 == 9`, else `val++`), one exported symbol, one branch, zero error returns.\n\n**Artifacts in `translation/`:** `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `check_features.sh`, `mutation_check.sh`, `tests/{common/mod.rs,valid_paths.rs,error_paths.rs,smoke.rs}`\n\n**Gates:**\n\n| gate | status |\n|---|---|\n| Symbol parity (`nm -D` diff, debug + release) | **empty diff**; `ldd -r` clean |\n| Phase B — 22/22 `CONFIGS.md` rows, randomized (fixed seed) | **pass** |\n| Phase C — 14/14 `ERRORS.md` rows | **pass** |\n| Binary stdout comparison | **N/A** — neither side builds an executable |\n| All feature combinations | **pass** (no `[features]` table; default / `--no-default-features` / `--all-features` each built, symbol-diffed, tested) |\n\n38 tests, 0 failures; also green against the optimized `panic=\"abort\"` release `.so`.\n\nBoth `.so`s are `dlopen`ed and driven through the exported `sieve` symbol only — never called directly — and outputs are compared as exact stdout bytes (fd-1 redirection), with forked-child 256 KiB prefix comparison for the inputs whose C output is unbounded.\n\nThree things a naive translation would get wrong, each pinned by a test:\n- **C truncated modulo** — `-9 % 10 == -9`, never `9`, so negatives never break early; `sieve(-9)` emits 19 lines, not 1.\n- **Signed overflow at `INT_MAX`** — C runs `val++` on `INT_MAX` (UB) and the `-O0` C wraps to `INT_MIN`; `wrapping_add` matches the observed stream. The boundary is sharp: `INT_MAX-8` terminates, `INT_MAX-7` never does.\n- **Platform `printf`** rather than Rust formatting, so buffering and field widths yield an identical byte stream.\n\nTwo notes on how I hardened the process:\n- I ran `mutation_check.sh` to confirm the suite has real detection power: **12/12 injected mistranslations detected**. The first attempt had 3 survivors — two were hangs the suite couldn't report and one was an equivalent (non-divergent) mutant. I fixed that by adding a watchdog that converts a non-terminating call into an attributed failure, capping the pipe reader, and replacing the bogus mutant. Detection is now by test-suite exit code, so hangs count.\n- During that mutation run a backup path outside the writable sandbox silently failed, so `src/lib.rs` briefly accumulated mutants. I restored it and byte-verified it against the original before the final run; `mutation_check.sh` now keeps its backup inside the crate and restores on exit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":768,"cache_read_input_tokens":110400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":768,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eea22903-d804-4bb4-aedc-2310b45c00a1","uuid":"66a018ae-0495-4fa6-991e-bf60f648419e","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:00:58.427Z"}
